PicoGKRuntime 26.2 (0f26321c) — bulk lattice authoring in the C ABI.

PROPOSAL, NOT APPLIED LOCALLY. picovoxel ships this as a sibling translation
unit (src/pico-bulk.cpp) so the vendored tree stays pristine; this file is the
same code shaped as a diff against upstream, for leap71/PicoGKRuntime. Ledger
row U17.

REPO SPLIT: this patch is the C ABI half only. The C# binding half —
Lattice.AddBeam/AddSphere accumulating into a flat float array and flushing once
per lattice instead of a P/Invoke per element — targets a DIFFERENT repository
(leap71/PicoGK) and is described in the U17 ledger row rather than diffed here.

Why: Lattice_AddBeam is the hottest ABI site in the port. One picovoxel fixture
(HelixHeatX) crosses it 1,197,460 times across 37 lattices; bulk transfer turns
that into 37 crossings. Facade cost 50.1 -> 39.2 ns/beam, `author` stage
238.7 -> 150.8 ms (paired ABAB x5), voxelization byte-identical. Evidence:
bench/results/webgpu-v2/SK-0.3.md. The C# binding has the same shape of problem.

Wire format is chosen for the GPU upload seam, not for this loop: 8 floats per
beam as (x, y, z, radius) per endpoint is two vec4 lanes at a 32-byte stride,
no padding under std140 or std430, so the same buffer a binding accumulates can
be handed to a GPU writeBuffer unrepacked. Round-cap flags ride in a parallel
uint32 array (WGSL has no u8, so a byte array would have to be widened anyway).

Elements still route through Lattice::AddBeam/AddSphere, which preserves the
bounding-box update and the degenerate round-cap rule — a zero-length
round-capped beam becomes a sphere (PicoGKLattice.h:213-218). Bulk-inserting
behind their back would change what gets rendered.

Note this patch does NOT change the storage: upstream keeps
std::vector<LatticeBeam::Ptr>, one make_shared per beam. That allocator cost is
20.9 ns/beam of the remaining 39.2 and is filed separately as ledger row U18.

Applies with `patch -p1` to a pristine PicoGKRuntime 0f26321c tree.

--- a/API/PicoGK.h
+++ b/API/PicoGK.h
@@ -201,6 +201,24 @@
                                                             float               fRadiusA,
                                                             float               fRadiusB,
                                                             bool                bRoundCap);
+
+// Bulk lattice authoring. pfBeams is a flat float array, 8 floats per beam:
+// (x0, y0, z0, r0, x1, y1, z1, r1) -- endpoint A then endpoint B, radius in the
+// w lane of each, so one beam is two vec4 lanes at a 32-byte stride and the same
+// buffer can be uploaded to a GPU unrepacked. pnRoundCap is one uint32 per beam
+// (0 = flat cone). pfSpheres is 4 floats per sphere, (x, y, z, radius) -- the
+// same lane shape as one beam endpoint. Both return the number appended.
+
+PICOGK_API int32_t          Lattice_AddBeams(               PKINSTANCE          hInstance,
+                                                            PKLATTICE           hThis,
+                                                            const float*        pfBeams,
+                                                            const uint32_t*     pnRoundCap,
+                                                            int32_t             nCount);
+
+PICOGK_API int32_t          Lattice_AddSpheres(             PKINSTANCE          hInstance,
+                                                            PKLATTICE           hThis,
+                                                            const float*        pfSpheres,
+                                                            int32_t             nCount);
 
 // VOXELS
 
--- a/Source/PicoGKLibrary.cpp
+++ b/Source/PicoGKLibrary.cpp
@@ -392,6 +392,60 @@
                     fRadiusA,
                     fRadiusB,
                     bRoundCap);
+}
+
+// Bulk lattice authoring -- the import mirror of the bulk mesh entry points.
+//
+// Lattice_AddBeam is a per-element ABI crossing, and a lattice is authored in
+// the hundreds of thousands of beams. Elements still route through
+// Lattice::AddBeam / AddSphere so the bounding box and the degenerate round-cap
+// rule (a zero-length round-capped beam becomes a sphere) are unchanged; the win
+// is not the loop, it is not crossing the ABI once per beam.
+
+PICOGK_API int32_t Lattice_AddBeams( PKINSTANCE hLib,
+                                     PKLATTICE hThis,
+                                     const float* pfBeams,
+                                     const uint32_t* pnRoundCap,
+                                     int32_t nCount)
+{
+    if (pfBeams == nullptr || pnRoundCap == nullptr || nCount <= 0)
+        return 0;
+
+    Library::Instance::Ptr roLib = Library::oLib().roGetInstance(hLib);
+    Lattice::Ptr roLattice = roLib->m_oLattices.roGet(hThis);
+
+    for (int32_t n = 0; n < nCount; n++)
+    {
+        const float* pf = pfBeams + n * 8;
+
+        roLattice->AddBeam( Vector3(pf[0], pf[1], pf[2]),
+                            Vector3(pf[4], pf[5], pf[6]),
+                            pf[3],
+                            pf[7],
+                            pnRoundCap[n] != 0);
+    }
+
+    return nCount;
+}
+
+PICOGK_API int32_t Lattice_AddSpheres(  PKINSTANCE hLib,
+                                        PKLATTICE hThis,
+                                        const float* pfSpheres,
+                                        int32_t nCount)
+{
+    if (pfSpheres == nullptr || nCount <= 0)
+        return 0;
+
+    Library::Instance::Ptr roLib = Library::oLib().roGetInstance(hLib);
+    Lattice::Ptr roLattice = roLib->m_oLattices.roGet(hThis);
+
+    for (int32_t n = 0; n < nCount; n++)
+    {
+        const float* pf = pfSpheres + n * 4;
+        roLattice->AddSphere(Vector3(pf[0], pf[1], pf[2]), pf[3]);
+    }
+
+    return nCount;
 }
 
